Here is the Manual Mapping Version of the same project.
This is actually better for learning because you can see exactly how data moves from one box to another. You don't need any external libraries (pom.xml dependencies) for this.
📦 Step 1: The DTOs (Public Data)
Stays exactly the same.
Input (UserRequest.java)
package org.example.demo1.dto;

import lombok.Data;

@Data
public class UserRequest {
    private String name;
    private String email;
    private String password; 
}

Output (UserResponse.java)
package org.example.demo1.dto;

import lombok.Data;

@Data
public class UserResponse {
    private Long id;
    private String name;
    private String email;
}

🗄️ Step 2: The Entity (Database Table)
Stays exactly the same.
package org.example.demo1.model;

import jakarta.persistence.*;
import lombok.Data;

@Entity
@Data
public class UserEntity {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
